          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            The Midea Cube is a good dehumidifier wrapped in a genuinely useful idea. The drying is the same as any ENERGY STAR unit of its size; what you are buying is a bucket big enough to cut trips, a fill level you can match to your back, and a shape that nests away for the winter. Buy the 35 for most homes, the 20 for one room and the 50 for a genuinely wet space.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Pay for the pump only if you cannot drain by gravity, and if you will run a hose to a floor drain all season, save money with Midea's conventional box or another 50 pint ENERGY STAR model. Whichever Cube you choose, keep the receipt: the warranty is one year, and the bucket weighs 40 pounds when full.
